{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Kruskal.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L21"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that order the minimum"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spanning forest is unique, and this is it. Its edges are listed in nondecreasing weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and, among equal weights, in position order, and the weight is added up in that order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sparse graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) run Kruskal’s algorithm; denser ones run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Prim’s under the same order and sort the edges taken."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop and is not kept. Negative, zero and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinite weights are ordinary weights. A NaN weight traps; filter such edges out first."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m log m).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not overflow and is not NaN."}]}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"]}],"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/SpanningForest":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpanningForest"}],"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/spanningforest",